  "description": "DINTAY crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C32 H74 Gd4 N4 Ni5 O46,4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ni1 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni5 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.068-3.868 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.26-113.51°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C36H90N4O50Ni5Gd4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 10 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
